{title: Amazing Grace (Graveson Version)}
{artist: Edwin Othello Excell; John Newton; John P. Rees; William W. Walker}
{key: Eb}
{ccli: 22025}
{meta: cant_key E}

{comment: Chorus 1}
[Eb]Amazing [Eb/G]Grace, how [Ab]sweet [Adim]the [Bb7]sound,
That [Eb]saved a [Cm7]wretch like [Bb7]me.[Bb7/C][Bb7/Db][Bb7/D]
I [Eb]once was [Eb/G]lost, [G7]but [Ab]now im [Bb7]found,
Was [Cm7]blind, but [Eb/Bb]now [Bb7]I [Ab/Eb]see.[Eb]

{comment: Chorus 2}
Twas [Eb]grace that [Eb/G]taught my [Ab]heart [Adim]to [Bb7]fear,
And [Eb]grace my [Cm7]fears [Bb7]relieved.
How [Eb]precious [Eb/G]did [G7]that [Ab]grace [Bb7]appear,
The [Cm7]hour I [Eb/Bb]first [Bb7]bel[Ab/Eb]ieved.[Eb]

{comment: Chorus 3}
Through [Eb]many [Eb/G]dangers, [Ab]toils [Adim]and [Bb7]snares
I [Eb]have [Cm7]already [Bb7]come.
T'was [Eb]Grace that [Eb/G]brought [G7]us [Ab]safe thus [Bb7]far
And [Cm7]Grace will [Eb/Bb]lead [Bb7]us [Ab/Eb]home.[Eb]

{comment: Chorus 4}
When [Eb]we've been [Eb/G]there ten [Ab]thou[Adim]sand [Bb7]years,
Bright [Eb]shining [Cm7]as the [Bb7]sun
we've [Eb]no less [Eb/G]days [G7]to [Ab]sing god's [Bb7]praise
Than [Cm7]when we [Eb/Bb]first [Bb7]beg[Ab/Eb]un.[Eb]
